{
  "about": "One admission refusal per code in the contract's table. Each refuses the whole request with an ERROR frame whose body is refusal ({code, message, detail}); detail.class carries the code's class, and the other detail members are the table's. An admission refusal writes nothing and calls no provider. batch_id_reuse assumes a recorded batch vec-refuse-reuse whose item 0 differs; replay-batch-id-reuse.json shows both calls. batch_in_progress assumes another call holds vec-refuse-busy. auth_failed and model_unavailable assume the call's first provider call (item 0) was answered 401 and 404: a 401 or 403, or a 404, met on the first provider call refuses the whole call at admission, so item 1 is never sent and nothing is recorded.",
  "refusals": [
    {
      "name": "invalid_params",
      "request": {
        "batch_id": "vec-refuse-invalid",
        "model": "cloudflare/clef",
        "questions": {
          "urgent": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "Is this support request urgent?"
          }
        },
        "items": [
          {
            "state": "Checkout has been failing for every customer for the last hour."
          },
          {
            "state": null
          }
        ]
      },
      "refusal": {
        "code": "invalid_params",
        "message": "state is a string, an object or an array",
        "detail": {
          "class": "permanent",
          "field": "items[1].state"
        }
      }
    },
